# Path ignores for the opengrep SAST scan in .github/workflows/scan.yaml.
#
# A .semgrepignore REPLACES the scanner's built-in default ignore list, so the defaults that
# matter are restated by including .gitignore (node_modules, build outputs, caches).
:include .gitignore
.git/

# Prose and generated reports. Several registry rules are bare regexes — e.g.
# javascript.lang.security.detect-insecure-websocket is `\bws://` with only localhost and
# 127.0.0.1 exempted — and match documentation the same as code. `ws://` is an accepted
# node-URL scheme here by design (src/config/core-settings.ts, NODE), so every mention in
# prose is a false positive. Code stays scanned; a flagged code line is suppressed on the
# line itself with `nosemgrep: <rule-id>`.
*.md
graphify-out/
